# CROSS-PLATFORM TESTING PROTOCOL: INFINITY PROTOCOL v6.2

> **VIEWPORT SOVEREIGNTY**: The application must remain uncompromised and fully functional across ALL viewports and accessibility boundaries. Broken mobile layouts are critical deployment blockers.

## 1. THE GOLDEN TRIANGLE — Required Test Targets
| Device | Browser | Viewport | Priority |
|---|---|---|---|
| iPhone 15 Pro | Mobile Safari | 393×852 | P0 |
| Samsung Galaxy S23 | Chrome Android | 360×780 | P0 |
| MacBook Pro 14" | Desktop Chrome | 1512×982 | P0 |

## 2. PLAYWRIGHT MOBILE CONFIGURATION
Your `playwright.config.ts` must implicitly define these exact devices.

```typescript
// ✅ REQUIRED PATTERN: playwright.config.ts
import { defineConfig, devices } from '@playwright/test';

export default defineConfig({
  projects: [
    { name: 'desktop-chrome', use: { ...devices['Desktop Chrome'] } },
    { name: 'desktop-safari', use: { ...devices['Desktop Safari'] } },
    { name: 'mobile-ios',     use: { ...devices['iPhone 15 Pro'] } },
    { name: 'mobile-android', use: { ...devices['Pixel 7'] } },
  ],
});
```

## 3. RESPONSIVE ASSERTION DISCIPLINE
Do NOT just test state; test *layout breakage*.

```typescript
// ✅ REQUIRED PATTERN: Responsive Assertions
import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('Mobile navigation remains accessible and does not overflow', async ({ page, isMobile }) => {
  await page.goto('/');

  // 1. No horizontal scroll allowed at any viewport
  const scrollWidth = await page.evaluate(() => document.documentElement.scrollWidth);
  const clientWidth = await page.evaluate(() => document.documentElement.clientWidth);
  expect(scrollWidth).toBe(clientWidth);

  if (isMobile) {
    // 2. Mobile touch target size validation (WCAG minimum 44x44)
    const hamburgerBtn = page.getByRole('button', { name: 'Open menu' });
    const box = await hamburgerBtn.boundingBox();
    expect(box?.height).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(44);
    expect(box?.width).toBeGreaterThanOrEqual(44);
  }
});
```

## 4. THEME & DARK MODE INVERSION
Test both light and dark systems in Playwright natively.

```typescript
// ✅ REQUIRED PATTERN: Dark Mode Emulation
test.use({ colorScheme: 'dark' });

test('Elements invert correctly in dark mode', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.goto('/dashboard');
  
  // Verify glassmorphism background adapted to dark theme
  const glassPanel = page.locator('.backdrop-blur-md').first();
  await expect(glassPanel).toHaveCSS('background-color', 'rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.4)'); // Expecting Dark Glass
});
```
